# Overrides the site-wide `immutable` caching from the root .htaccess for this
# folder only.
#
# Everything under /assets/ carries a content hash in its filename (Docusaurus
# and the ideal-image plugin put it there), so a changed file always means a
# changed URL and caching it for a year is safe. The 300+ files here are the
# opposite: they are copied verbatim from static/img/, keeping the name I gave
# them. Replacing a banner image in place therefore leaves returning visitors
# looking at last year's copy for up to a year.
#
# A week is the compromise: still cached hard enough to cost nothing on repeat
# visits, short enough that an image swap actually reaches readers. Use a new
# filename when a change must be visible immediately.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  <FilesMatch "\.(png|jpg|jpeg|webp|avif|gif|svg|ico)$">
    Header set Cache-Control "public, max-age=604800, must-revalidate"
  </FilesMatch>
</IfModule>
